MIT-licensed code ported from another project.

1. ASD-STE100 extracted material
---------------------------------

This repository contains material extracted from ASD-STE100 Issue 9
(2025-01-15), "Simplified Technical English", copyright (c) ASD 2025.

That material lives in:

  - docs/ASD-STE100-rules-extracted.md
  - docs/incidents/2026-08-01-ste100-dictionary-extraction-gate-bypass.dat
  - src/rulesets/ste100/dictionary.json (built from the .dat file above)

This is not the author's own work and is not covered by this repository's
MIT license (see LICENSE). It is included under the ASD-STE100 usage
rights that apply to this repository's owning entity. If you plan to
reuse this content outside this project, check your own standing under
the ASD-STE100 licensing terms first -- do not assume this repository's
inclusion of the material extends any right to you.

The extraction was verified against the source PDF before being trusted
as enforcement data; see src/rulesets/ste100/build_dictionary.py's docstring for
the verification method, and docs/incidents/ for the incident this
verification step responds to.

2. Ported MIT-licensed code
----------------------------

src/rulesets/ste100/lint.py ports two checks from SimpleEnglish
(https://github.com/AminBlg/SimpleEnglish), file evals/ste_lint.py:

  - TRAILING_COND / check_trailing_condition() -- the condition-before-
    command check (rules 5.4/7.2)
  - the base of ROTATION_SETS / check_synonym_rotation() -- the one-term-
    per-concept check (rules 1.11/9.4). This repository added three more
    rotation sets (delete-remove, run-execute, show-display) beyond
    SimpleEnglish's original two.

